Project project_schema {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: '''
  Authoritative physical data contract for one database. Tables, columns,
  types, nullability, defaults, keys, indexes, references, and
  database-enforced constraints live here. ENT artifacts own domain meaning;
  interface files own wire representations. Sibling *.dbml files in this
  directory are discovered as further SCHEMA-* contracts, one per database;
  an entity in a multi-file repository names its owning file in depends_on.
  The empty draft is intentional until active entities require persistence.
  '''
}

// Completion contract before a schema-backed feature is active:
// - Every table and column maps to an ENT attribute/relationship or documented
//   technical necessity.
// - Tenant/organization ownership columns, foreign keys, and access-supporting
//   indexes make the isolation model explicit where applicable.
// - Requiredness, defaults, uniqueness, referential actions, and constraints
//   agree with entity states/invariants and write-processing designs.
// - Sensitive fields are minimized and map to retention/deletion rules.
// - Indexes name the query/invariant they support; speculative indexes are absent.
// - Compatibility/backfill consequences are recorded in ENT mapping and ADR when
//   the physical change has a durable tradeoff.

// Native-comment shape for a future concrete table (guidance, not schema):
// Table <semantic_plural_name> {
//   id <database_type> [pk, note: '<ENT-ID>#<attribute-ID>']
//   <tenant_key> <database_type> [not null]
//   <attribute> <database_type> [not null, note: '<ENT-ID>#<attribute-ID>']
//   created_at timestamp [not null]
//   updated_at timestamp [not null]
//
//   indexes {
//     (<tenant_key>, <attribute>) [name: '<meaningful_index_name>']
//   }
//
//   Note: '<ENT-ID>; writes owned by <API/JOB/SUB-ID>'
// }
// Ref: <child_table>.<foreign_key> > <parent_table>.id
